  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/7FD2F6">Proposition <span data-tag="7FD2F6">7.1.1.1</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a paracompact topological space and $U$ an open subset of $X$. The following conditions are equivalent: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(i)$"><p>
There exists a continuous function $f: X \rightarrow [0,1]$ such that $U = \{  x \in X: f(x) > 0 \} $. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(ii)$"><p>
There exists a sequence of closed subsets $\{  K_{n} \subseteq X \} _{n \geq 0}$ such that each $K_{n+1}$ contains an open neighborhood of $K_{n}$, and $U = \bigcup _{n \geq 0} K_ n$. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(iii)$"><p>
There exists a sequence of closed subsets $\{  K_{n} \subseteq X \} _{n \geq 0}$ such that $U = \bigcup _{n \geq 0} K_ n$. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
  <p> Let $\calB $ denote the collection of all open subsets of $X$ which satisfy these conditions. Then: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
The elements of $\calB $ form a basis for the topology of $X$. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
Each element of $\calB $ is paracompact. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(3)$"><p>
The collection $\calB $ is stable under finite intersections (in particular, $X \in \calB $). 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(4)$"><p>
The empty set $\emptyset $ belongs to $\calB $. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
